__pycache__/
*.pyc
# The database is not committed: it is a 7MB binary that changes every hour,
# and git stores a whole new copy each time - about 2.7GB a month. The same
# information lives in data/shards as plain text that is only ever added to,
# which git stores for the cost of the lines added, and which `archive
# restore` turns back into a database.
data/ingest.sqlite
data/*.sqlite-wal
data/*.sqlite-shm
data/view.html
data/cacert.pem
.venv/
.env
.env.*
